hbsetbg
=======

The Tool that is used to set the XLibre desktop background in Hackedbox.
It can load an image using several placement modes. It is intended specifically for setting the desktop/root-window background.

Usage:
    hbsetbg [option] <path to image>

Options

    -center, --center <image>
        Display the image at its original size, centered on the screen.

    -tile, --tile <image>
        Tile the image across the entire screen.

    -s2c, --stretch2center <image>
        Scale the image proportionally so that it fits within the screen,
        then center it.

    -s2e, --stretch2edge <image>
        Scale the image proportionally to cover the screen.
        The image may extend beyond the screen edges.
        


It is built as part of Hackedbox and is used internally by the
Hackedbox style/background system. Users normally do not need to
invoke hbsetbg directly.

Backgrounds are configured through the Hackedbox style configuration.
When a style specifies a root background, Hackedbox invokes hbsetbg
behind the scenes to apply the requested background.

Style properties include:

    root.background
    root.background.mode
    root.background.folder
    root.background.timer

The style system is responsible for determining when and how hbsetbg
is used.

Purpose
-------

hbsetbg provides the actual background-setting functionality while
keeping background configuration inside the Hackedbox style system.

This separates:

    Style configuration
        ↓
    Hackedbox / HbTK style handling
        ↓
    hbsetbg
        ↓
    X11/XLibre root window

The utility therefore remains a separate executable internally, but
is not intended to be part of the normal user-facing configuration
workflow.

Status
------

hbsetbg was developed from the ground up for Hackedbox and replaces
the need for users to manually manage the root background through
external background-setting commands.

Direct invocation may still be possible for development/debugging,
but normal operation is handled automatically by Hackedbox.
